@startuml SD_AutomaticVehicleFault
title FR-NI-01/02/07 - Automatic vehicle-fault handling
hide footbox
autonumber
actor "External Telemetry Provider\n(or mock timer)" as Source
boundary "Telemetry Gateway" as G
control "TelemetryController" as C
entity "VehicleRepository" as V
entity "IncidentRepository" as I
entity "AssignmentRepository" as A
entity "AlertStore" as L

Source -> G: Send vehicle ID, timestamp, condition, battery
G -> C: ingestTelemetry(event)
C -> V: Load vehicle and latest accepted timestamp
V --> C: Current state and timestamp
alt Invalid ID, missing fields, duplicate or stale event
  C --> G: Reject or ignore with reason
else Valid newer event
  C -> V: Apply observation and freshness timestamp
  opt Fault or ineligible condition reported
    C -> V: Restrict new allocations
    C -> I: Find equivalent open vehicle incident
    alt Equivalent incident exists
      I --> C: Existing ticket
      C -> I: Append new evidence once
    else No equivalent incident exists
      I --> C: None
      C -> I: Create Reported ticket
    end
    C -> A: Find incomplete assignments containing vehicle
    loop Each affected assignment
      C -> A: Mark AtRisk with conflict reason
    end
    C -> L: Publish fault and assignment alerts
  end
  C --> G: Accepted state and incident reference
end
note over C,L
No Operator click is required. Repeated fault events do not create
duplicate open tickets or confirm physical redistribution.
end note
@enduml
